1
00:07:56,250 --> 00:08:02,250
The History of Sound is a drama, romance, music
film directed by Oliver Hermanus.

2
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:58,500
In 1917, two young music students attending the Boston
Conservatory bond over a mutual love of folk music.

3
00:23:48,750 --> 00:23:54,750
They reconnect a few years later, embarking on a
song-collecting trip in the backwaters of Maine.

4
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Lionel, played by Paul Mescal.

5
00:39:41,250 --> 00:39:47,250
David, played by Josh O'Connor.

6
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:43,500
Lionel's Mother, played by Molly Price.

7
00:55:33,750 --> 00:55:39,750
Samantha, played by Alison Bartlett.

8
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
Bob, played by Michael Schantz.

9
01:11:26,250 --> 01:11:32,250
Older Lionel, played by Chris Cooper.

10
01:19:22,500 --> 01:19:28,500
The History of Sound is a 2025 period romance drama film directed by Oliver Hermanus, written by Ben
Shattuck, and based on a pair of his short stories: "The History of Sound" and "Origin Stories".

11
01:27:18,750 --> 01:27:24,750
It follows the relationship between two men, Lionel (Paul Mescal) and David (Josh O'Connor), who meet in 1917 while attending the New England
Conservatory of Music, and after World War I travel together recording folk songs of their countrymen in rural Maine in the winter of 1920.

12
01:35:15,000 --> 01:35:21,000
The film had its world premiere at the 2025 Cannes Film Festival on
May 21, where it was nominated for the Palme d'Or.

13
01:43:11,250 --> 01:43:17,250
It was released in the United States by Mubi on September 12.

14
01:51:07,500 --> 01:51:13,500
The film explores themes of world war i, boston,
massachusetts, conservatory, folk music, road trip.

15
01:59:03,750 --> 01:59:09,750
The tone is emotional.
